One thing I'd really love to see for a new version of hack would be
a new feature for teleport control.  Namely, if you're selecting where
to teleport, instead of aiming using the number pad, you can type
'>' or '<' to teleport directly to the up or down stairs.  If the
location of desired stairs are unknown, these keys should do nothing.
If there is a mimic mimicking stairs, '<' or '>' may try to land you
on top of him (and fail).  Note that this does not change the nature of
teleport control.  It just makes it faster for the player to draaaag
his cursor to where the stairs are.  With this, going up or down can
be done quickly.  If you know where all the stairs are, it's just
(cntl-t) (>) (>) (cntl-t) (>) (>) ... 
to dive an arbitrary number of levels.  This would improve playing
speed a great deal.

Another nice feature would be inventory selection.  When dealing with
your inventory or a BIG pile, the player should be able to pick up
or drop an item just by getting a the list and running a cursor to
the appropriate item(s).  If this isn't feasible, it would be nice to,
at the very least, have a way to reverse when going through a pile.
Pick up a blessed +3 broadsword named Stormbringer? [ynqb]

This will put an end to the heart-wrenching cases where you go through
a pile for a minute and then miss the item you want by 1.

